            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-39373",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "JWCrypto: python-cryptography: python: JWCrypto: Memory exhaustion via crafted compressed JWE tokens"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "JWCrypto implements JWK, JWS, and JWE specifications using python-cryptography. Prior to 1.5.7, an unauthenticated attacker can exhaust server memory by sending crafted JWE tokens with ZIP compression. The existing patch for CVE-2024-28102  limits input token size to 250KB but does not validate the decompressed output size. An unauthenticated attacker can cause memory exhaustion on memory-constrained systems. A token under the 250KB input limit can decompress to approximately 100MB. This vulnerability is fixed in 1.5.7."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-39373",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-39373\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: jwcrypto\nFixed Version: 1.5.7\nLink: [CVE-2026-39373](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-39373)\nJWCrypto implements JWK, JWS, and JWE specifications using python-cryptography. Prior to 1.5.7, an unauthenticated attacker can exhaust server memory by sending crafted JWE tokens with ZIP compression. The existing patch for CVE-2024-28102  limits input token size to 250KB but does not validate the decompressed output size. An unauthenticated attacker can cause memory exhaustion on memory-constrained systems. A token under the 250KB input limit can decompress to approximately 100MB. This vulnerability is fixed in 1.5.7.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-39373**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|jwcrypto|1.5.7|[CVE-2026-39373](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-39373)|\n\nJWCrypto implements JWK, JWS, and JWE specifications using python-cryptography. Prior to 1.5.7, an unauthenticated attacker can exhaust server memory by sending crafted JWE tokens with ZIP compression. The existing patch for CVE-2024-28102  limits input token size to 250KB but does not validate the decompressed output size. An unauthenticated attacker can cause memory exhaustion on memory-constrained systems. A token under the 250KB input limit can decompress to approximately 100MB. This vulnerability is fixed in 1.5.7."
              },
